<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Munster</h1><p class="st-meta">400 CE – 1118 CE (approx.) · capital Cashel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Southern Irish over-kingdom ruled from the Rock of Cashel by the Eóganachta and later by the Dál Cais of Brian Bóruma, until it split in two in 1118.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Munster, Mumu in Irish, was one of the ancient provinces of Ireland. From around the 5th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganachta</a> dynasties, tracing descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conall-corc">Conall Corc</a>, the legendary founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rock-of-cashel">Cashel</a>, established an over-kingship over the province, displacing earlier <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/iverni">Érainn</a> peoples such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcu-loigde">Corcu Loigde</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rock-of-cashel">Cashel</a> through a confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganacht</a> branches, collecting tribute from many subject peoples. Several were also churchmen or patrons of learning, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feidlimid-mac-crimthainn">Feidlimid mac Crimthainn</a>, king and abbot, who died in 847. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cathal-mac-finguine">Cathal mac Finguine</a>, who died in 742, challenged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> for supremacy. In the 10th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-cais">Dál Cais of Thomond</a> took the kingship, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Bóruma</a>, king of Munster from 978, became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-king-of-ireland">High King of Ireland</a> in 1002.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1101 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muirchertach-ua-briain">Muirchertach Ua Briain</a> gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rock-of-cashel">Rock of Cashel</a> to the Church. In 1118 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toirdelbach-ua-conchobair">Toirdelbach Ua Conchobair</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Kingdom of Connacht</a> divided Munster by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-glanmire">Treaty of Glanmire</a> into Desmond, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthys</a>, and Thomond, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrien-dynasty">O'Briens</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-munster.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Munster" width="320" height="418"><figcaption>Image: Erigena · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Munster-900.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 CE – 1118 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cashel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cathal mac Finguine, Feidlimid mac Crimthainn, Brian Bóruma</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish, later Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mumu, Munster, Kingdom of Cashel</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=759&amp;focus=kingdom-of-munster" aria-label="Kingdom of Munster on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4503 366 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Munster lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4823 622L4799 613M4823 622L4786 635M4823 622L4786 635M4823 622L4838 618M4823 622L4840 629M4823 622L4807 618M4823 622L4823 606"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4799 613h0M4786 635h0M4786 635h0M4838 618h0M4840 629h0M4807 618h0M4823 606h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4823 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4823 622h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cashel. <a href="/atlas?year=759&amp;focus=kingdom-of-munster">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
